  "label": "Dehumanizing comparison through water context exploitation",
  "description": "The secondary mapping that compares children playing in water to Sea-Monkeys 'coming to life' when added to water further reinforces the racist dehumanization. This mapping exploits the aquatic setting to strengthen the comparison of Black children to toy organisms/pets, adding another layer of dehumanization by suggesting they are like products that 'activate' in water.",
